Run migrations from the `signal-mvp` project directory after configuring `.env`
and activating its virtual environment:

```shell
alembic upgrade head
```

The migration at `f13d9a2c6b80` seeds the bundled synthetic canonical
dataset with 333 patients (332 Synthea records and one SIGNAL demo record),
plus their canonical encounters, conditions, observations, lab results,
synthetic documents, candidates, and cases. The follow-up migration
`a74c8d1e2f30` adds three explicitly synthetic canonical demo patients. A clean
setup therefore starts with 336 canonical patients; subsequently ingested
records are counted as well. Both migrations are safe to reapply and do not
replace existing rows. The user-uploaded document is not included.
